comments.body:
@participant4 thank you for the careful investigation!

> This is definitely a hyprland-caused issue

Does this mean that this is a Hyprland _bug_, or that these intentional changes broke Wezterm (but shouldn't be reversed)?

> Is this fixed in wezterm-nightly or not? Is it related to any of the other Hyprland related issues in wezterm? And does Hyprland need to make this fix or does wezterm need to make it?

@participant7 This is not fixed (as of 3 days ago when I tried it last). As mentioned here https://github.com/wez/wezterm/issues/5067#issuecomment-1963238274, this is a wlroots spec update, meaning that this should be handled by wezterm.

I have moved to alacritty for the time being, as this, alongside #5079 make wezterm essentially unusable for me.
